Environment

Environment: Production (public demo site)
URL: https://www.saucedemo.com/checkout-step-two.html
Build / Version: index-DnLqFcJI.js
Device: Desktop
OS: Windows 11
Browser: Chrome
User role / Test account: standard_user

Description
On the Checkout: Overview page, “Item total” isn’t rounded to 2 decimals. For some product combinations, the browser’s decimal maths produces a long number, so the page shows amounts like “$59.980000000000004” instead of “$59.98”. This happens for 18 different product combinations. The “Generate PDF order” receipt rounds the same value correctly, so the page and the receipt show different item totals.

Preconditions

User is logged in as standard_user.
The cart is empty.

Steps to Reproduce

Log in as standard_user.
Click “Add to cart” on Sauce Labs Bike Light ($9.99) and Sauce Labs Fleece Jacket ($49.99).
Open the cart and click “Checkout”.
Enter First Name, Last Name and Zip/Postal Code, then click “Continue”.
Look at “Item total” on the Checkout: Overview page.

Test Data
These combinations all show a long decimal “Item total”:

Bike Light + Fleece Jacket: shows $59.980000000000004 (should be $59.98)
Onesie + Fleece Jacket: shows $57.980000000000004 (should be $57.98)
Bike Light + Bolt T-Shirt + Onesie + Backpack: shows $63.959999999999994 (should be $63.96)
Bike Light + Bolt T-Shirt + Onesie + Fleece Jacket: shows $83.96000000000001 (should be $83.96)
Bike Light + Bolt T-Shirt + Test.allTheThings() T-Shirt (Red) + Fleece Jacket: shows $91.96000000000001 (should be $91.96)
Bolt T-Shirt + Onesie + Test.allTheThings() T-Shirt (Red) + Fleece Jacket: shows $89.96000000000001 (should be $89.96)
12 more combinations do the same.

Actual Result

“Item total” shows “$59.980000000000004” for Bike Light + Fleece Jacket.
Tax ($4.80) and Total ($64.78) are rounded correctly, so only “Item total” is wrong.
The PDF receipt from “Generate PDF order” shows “Item total $59.98” for the same order, which doesn’t match the page.

Expected Result

“Item total” is always shown with exactly 2 decimals, for example “$59.98”.
The Overview page and the PDF receipt show the same amounts.

Reproducibility

Always for the combinations above (worked out from the code) [To confirm in the browser]

Impact

Affects all users who buy one of these 18 combinations.
A wrong-looking price on the payment summary hurts trust and can make users think they’re being overcharged.
Workaround: None.

Attachments
https://www.awesomescreenshot.com/image/64742790?key=d90a5cac5d11381d47d38a2a8b5aa777
Suggested Fix (optional)

Show “Item total” with toFixed(2), the same as Tax and Total.
Better: do the price maths in cents (whole numbers) to avoid decimal errors.

Acceptance Criteria

 Given the cart has Bike Light + Fleece Jacket, when the user opens Checkout: Overview, then “Item total” shows “$59.98”.
 Given any combination of the 6 products, when the user opens Checkout: Overview, then “Item total”, “Tax” and “Total” all show exactly 2 decimals.
 Given a finished order, when the user clicks “Generate PDF order”, then the PDF amounts match the Overview page.
